🔹 1. What are semantic HTML tags?
Semantic tags describe meaning of content, improving SEO & accessibility.
<header>, <nav>, <article>, <section>, <footer>, <aside
🔹 2. Difference between id and class ?
id: unique, used for a single element (#idSelector in CSS).
class: reusable, multiple elements can share it (.classSelector in CSS).

🔹 5. What are meta tags in HTML? 
Provide metadata (data about data) for web pages.
Not displayed directly, but used by browsers/search engines.

🔹 6. Difference between <div> and <span> ?
<div>: block-level container.
<span>: inline-level container.

🔹 12. What is difference between localStorage, sessionStorage, and cookies in HTML5?
localStorage: stores data with no expiration (until cleared).
sessionStorage: stores data for a session (cleared on tab close).
cookies: small pieces of data sent with HTTP requests, can expire.